    "compiled_date": "2026-07-29",
    "notes": "Alaska's Private Non-Profit (PNP) salmon hatchery system was authorized by the Alaska Legislature in 1974 (AS 16.10.375) following severe natural run failures in the early 1970s. Today, 30 PNP hatcheries release ~1.8 billion juvenile salmon annually (primarily pink and chum salmon). Hatchery-origin fish account for 25-35% of Alaska's total commercial salmon harvest value, generating $250M-$380M in ex-vessel value annually and supporting 4,500+ commercial fishing and processing jobs."
  },
